---
/**
 * /adms/support - how to get help.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const B = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Support"
  description="How to get help with ADMS: email support, release notes, documentation, and incident response."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        ADMS is maintained by Adapdev directly. When something breaks,
        the person who fixes it is the person who shipped it.
      </p>

      <h2>Email support</h2>
      <p>
        For general questions, bug reports, and feature requests, email
        support via the Adapdev website
        <a href="/contact">contact form</a>. Expect a reply within one
        Australian business day (Monday to Friday, Eastern time).
      </p>
      <p>
        When reporting a bug, please include your ADMS version
        (<em>Help &rarr; About</em> in the desktop client, or the
        <code>Server-Version</code> response header from the API), the
        operating system, and the sequence of actions that produced the
        issue.
      </p>

      <h2>Release notes and updates</h2>
      <p>
        Every ADMS release is documented in the
        <a href={`${B}/release-notes`}>release notes</a>. The
        <a href={`${B}/release-notes/rss.xml`}>RSS feed</a> is the
        recommended way to be notified of a new release without being
        on anyone's mailing list.
      </p>

      <h2>Security disclosures</h2>
      <p>
        Found a security issue? Please report it privately via the
        <a href="/contact">contact form</a> with "SECURITY" in the subject
        line, rather than opening a public GitHub issue. We follow a
        responsible-disclosure process in line with the Australian
        Notifiable Data Breaches scheme; see our incident-response
        procedure for timing and detail.
      </p>

      <h2>On-site assistance (law firms, metro AU)</h2>
      <p>
        For law-firm customers in metropolitan Australia, on-site
        onboarding and incident response are available. Travel is
        charged separately; see the <a href={`${B}/pricing`}>pricing
        page</a> for the base tier or get in touch for a quote.
      </p>

      <h2>Documentation</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Searchable product documentation is coming to this site. In the
        meantime, the ADMS installer ships with an offline operations
        manual (<code>%ProgramFiles%\Adapdev\ADMS\docs</code>) covering
        installation, backup, restore, rotation of signing keys, and
        the incident-response runbook.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .section { padding-block: var(--space-7); }
  .prose { max-width: 72ch; }
  .lede { font-size: var(--fs-lg); }
</style>
